            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">Total Disability Benefit</div><div class="b-val">$100 weekly for total disability · maximum 26 weeks. Begins after a 7-day elimination period.</div></div>
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">Emergency Accident</div><div class="b-val">Up to $100 for outpatient ER treatment within 72 hours. Not payable if other benefits apply.</div></div>
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">AD&D — Regular Accident</div><div class="b-val">$10,000 full loss / $5,000 partial loss</div></div>
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">AD&D — Auto Accident</div><div class="b-val">$25,000 full loss / $12,500 partial loss</div></div>
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">AD&D — Common Carrier</div><div class="b-val">$50,000 full loss / $25,000 partial loss</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Key Differences vs. A71</div>
          <p>The A74 trades the daily hospital benefit and ICU doubler for a weekly disability income benefit — a fundamentally different value proposition focused on income continuity rather than hospitalization costs. The ER benefit improves from $50 to $100. The AD&D structure shifts from percentage multipliers to fixed tiered dollar amounts, providing maximum clarity for clients. Drugs and narcotics exclusion is slightly more lenient on A74 (excludes use unless prescribed by a physician).</p>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Exclusions & Limitations</div>
          <ul class="exclusion-list">
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Suicide or intentional self-inflicted injury, while sane or insane</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>War or act of war, declared or undeclared; military service in any country</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Air travel, except as fare-paying passenger on a regularly scheduled commercial airline</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Any type of hernia</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Racing contests, skydiving, or other hazardous avocations</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Use of drugs or narcotics unless taken as prescribed by a physician</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Use of hallucinogens</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Sickness, illness, disease, or mental illness</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Committing or attempting to commit a felony or assault</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Agent Field Notes</div>
          <div class="key-points">
            <div class="kp-title">Sales Positioning</div>
            <ul class="kp-list">
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>Lead with the disability income — "If you're hurt and can't work, this pays you $100 per week for up to six months while you recover"</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>Set the 7-day elimination period expectation proactively — clients should understand week one falls on them</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>The $50,000 common carrier AD&D ceiling is extraordinarily high relative to premium cost and should be featured prominently</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>Optimal for blue-collar workers, tradespeople, delivery personnel, or anyone whose income depends on physical capacity</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- C10 -->
    <div class="deep-card" id="deep-c10" style="--product-color: var(--c10)">
      <div class="deep-card-header" onclick="toggleDeep('c10')">
        <div class="deep-badge">C10</div>
        <div class="deep-meta">
          <h2>Cancer Indemnity (Daily) — Form C10000</h2>
          <p>Daily cash benefit throughout cancer treatment · Hospital & outpatient coverage</p>
        </div>
        <div class="deep-chevron">▾</div>
      </div>
      <div class="deep-body">

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Policy Overview</div>
          <p>The C10 is a daily-benefit cancer indemnity policy — it pays for every day the insured is confined in a hospital or actively receiving qualifying outpatient cancer treatment. Unlike lump-sum cancer products, C10 sustains clients financially throughout extended treatment regimens that may span six months to two years. The daily benefit amount is established at policy issue. A separate Government Hospital daily benefit applies for confinement in VA or other US Government facilities.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Complete Benefits Schedule</div>
          <div class="benefit-grid">
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">Hospital Confinement</div><div class="b-val">$___ per day (set at issue) · lifetime maximum 500 days · not payable in US Government hospitals</div></div>
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">Outpatient Treatment</div><div class="b-val">$___ per day (same rate as hospital) · lifetime maximum 500 days · covers: surgery, cobalt therapy, X-ray therapy, blood transfusions, chemotherapy</div></div>
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">Government Hospital</div><div class="b-val">Separate daily benefit rate for confinement in US Government-operated hospitals · 500-day lifetime maximum</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Eligibility Rules & Waiting Period</div>
          <p>The client and all covered family members must have no prior cancer diagnosis. The policy carries a 30-day waiting period from the effective date — any cancer diagnosed within 30 days results in no coverage for that person and a full premium refund. Benefits are not payable for treatment received more than 90 days prior to the required pathological diagnosis. Clinical diagnosis is accepted only when medical judgment prohibits pathological procedures and other conclusive evidence is provided.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Optional Rider — BH-102 Cancer Detection</div>
          <p>Provides a single-sum benefit upon first cancer diagnosis. Skin cancer receives a reduced lump-sum amount; all other cancers receive the full rider benefit. When combined with C10, this creates a hybrid product: an upfront diagnosis lump sum plus ongoing daily benefits throughout treatment — a comprehensive cancer financial protection package.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Agent Field Notes</div>
          <div class="key-points">
            <div class="kp-title">Sales Positioning</div>
            <ul class="kp-list">
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>"Chemotherapy regimens typically run six to eighteen months — this policy pays you every single day you go in for treatment"</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>Outpatient coverage is increasingly critical — the majority of modern cancer treatment occurs in outpatient settings, not hospitals</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>Pair with the BH-102 rider to deliver both an immediate lump sum at diagnosis and sustained daily benefits throughout treatment</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>Always disclose the 30-day waiting period clearly: "Coverage activates 30 days after the policy effective date"</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>The 500-day cap applies independently to hospital and outpatient — both categories carry their own 500-day ceiling</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- C20 -->
    <div class="deep-card" id="deep-c20" style="--product-color: var(--c20)">
      <div class="deep-card-header" onclick="toggleDeep('c20')">
        <div class="deep-badge">C20</div>
        <div class="deep-meta">
          <h2>Cancer First Diagnosis — Form C20000</h2>
          <p>Single lump-sum benefit at first cancer diagnosis · Coverage terminates at payout</p>
        </div>
        <div class="deep-chevron">▾</div>
      </div>
      <div class="deep-body">

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Policy Overview</div>
          <p>The C20 is AIL's simplest cancer product in structure — a single lump-sum payment upon first diagnosis of cancer, after which the policy terminates. Its value proposition is immediacy: at the moment of diagnosis, before treatment decisions are finalized, the client receives a cash benefit to address the financial disruption that precedes formal medical costs — specialist consultations, travel, lost income, childcare, and household continuity.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">The Benefit</div>
          <p>A single lump-sum amount established at policy issuance. Coverage terminates upon payment of the benefit. There are no recurring or daily benefits — the product pays once and is fulfilled. The specific dollar amount is filled in on the policy at time of issue.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Diagnoses Excluded from Coverage</div>
          <ul class="exclusion-list">
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Skin cancer of any type</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Carcinoma in Situ</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Stage 1 of Hodgkin's Disease</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Stage A Prostate Cancer</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Melanoma diagnosed as Clark's Level I or II, or Breslow measurement below .75 mm</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Eligibility, Age Reductions & Renewability</div>
          <p>No prior cancer history for the insured or any covered family member. 30-day waiting period; diagnosis within the first 30 days results in no coverage and full premium refund. Benefits reduce at age 65 — this is a material disclosure for clients approaching that age bracket. Policy is guaranteed renewable to age 80, with rate increases applied only on a statewide class basis.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Agent Field Notes</div>
          <div class="key-points">
            <div class="kp-title">Sales Positioning</div>
            <ul class="kp-list">
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>"At the moment of diagnosis, most families immediately face travel costs, time off work, childcare — this places cash in your hands before the first treatment bill arrives"</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>The simplicity is a feature: "You receive a cancer diagnosis — we send you a check. That's the entire product."</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>Stack with CI for comprehensive first-event coverage: C20 handles cancer, CI handles heart/stroke</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>The age-65 benefit reduction must be disclosed proactively, especially for clients in their late fifties</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>The skin cancer exclusion is frequently misunderstood — always address it explicitly before the client asks</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CI -->
    <div class="deep-card" id="deep-ci" style="--product-color: var(--ci)">
      <div class="deep-card-header" onclick="toggleDeep('ci')">
        <div class="deep-badge">CI</div>
        <div class="deep-meta">
          <h2>Critical Illness — Form CI0000</h2>
          <p>Lump-sum benefit for heart attack, stroke & five other critical events · Cancer excluded</p>
        </div>
        <div class="deep-chevron">▾</div>
      </div>
      <div class="deep-body">

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Policy Overview</div>
          <p>The Critical Illness policy mirrors C20 in structural design — one lump-sum payout at first diagnosis — but addresses the non-cancer critical illness spectrum. Heart attack and stroke represent the most statistically likely triggers. The policy is explicitly designed to complement C20: together, CI and C20 provide complete first-event lump-sum coverage across the two dominant categories of major health events that financially devastate American families.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Covered Critical Illnesses</div>
          <div class="benefit-grid">
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">Heart Attack</div><div class="b-val">First diagnosis while policy in force</div></div>
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">Stroke</div><div class="b-val">First diagnosis while policy in force</div></div>
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">End Stage Renal Failure</div><div class="b-val">First diagnosis while policy in force</div></div>
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">Major Organ Transplant</div><div class="b-val">First diagnosis while policy in force</div></div>
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">Total Loss of Hearing</div><div class="b-val">First diagnosis while policy in force</div></div>
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">Total Loss of Eyesight</div><div class="b-val">First diagnosis while policy in force</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Critical Policy Conditions</div>
          <p>30-day waiting period from policy date. Any covered critical illness manifesting within the first 30 days is not payable. First diagnosis must be made within the United States — diagnoses rendered outside the US are not covered. Benefit amount is reduced by 50% after age 65, which is the most significant age-related provision in the supplemental portfolio. Guaranteed renewable to age 80 with class-level rate adjustment authority only.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Exclusions & Limitations</div>
          <ul class="exclusion-list">
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Participation in an assault, felony, riot, or insurrection</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Mental or emotional disorders</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Suicide or intentional self-inflicted injury, while sane or insane</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>War or any act of war, declared or undeclared; military service</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Under influence of alcohol or any drug or narcotic unless prescribed by a physician</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Cancer of any kind (covered separately under C10 or C20)</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>First diagnosis made outside the United States of America</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Agent Field Notes</div>
          <div class="key-points">
            <div class="kp-title">Sales Positioning</div>
            <ul class="kp-list">
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>"Cardiovascular disease remains the leading cause of death in America — this places a check in your hands at the moment of diagnosis, before a single treatment bill arrives"</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>Always present CI alongside C20: "One policy covers cancer. The other covers heart attacks and strokes. Together they address the two most financially devastating health events a family faces."</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>The US-only diagnosis requirement is worth raising with clients who travel internationally or have family abroad</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>The 50% age-65 reduction is the most impactful age provision in the portfolio — disclose it clearly, early, and unprompted</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>The policy pays once and terminates — position it as providing financial flexibility and immediate relief, not as ongoing treatment support</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- H34 -->
    <div class="deep-card" id="deep-h34" style="--product-color: var(--h34)">
      <div class="deep-card-header" onclick="toggleDeep('h34')">
        <div class="deep-badge">H34</div>
        <div class="deep-meta">
          <h2>Hospital Confinement Indemnity — Form H34007</h2>
          <p>Any-cause hospital daily cash · Outpatient surgery · At-home recovery benefit · Non-cancellable for life</p>
        </div>
        <div class="deep-chevron">▾</div>
      </div>
      <div class="deep-body">

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Policy Overview</div>
          <p>The H34 is the most versatile product in the supplemental portfolio — providing daily hospital indemnity for any covered cause of confinement, whether accident or sickness. Unlike every other supplemental, it does not restrict coverage to a single event type. It uniquely incorporates outpatient surgical indemnity, an At-Home recovery benefit, and accidental death and dismemberment coverage. The renewal guarantee is unmatched: the company cannot cancel this policy under any circumstances, providing lifetime hospital protection.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Complete Benefits Schedule</div>
          <div class="benefit-grid">
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">In-Hospital Indemnity</div><div class="b-val">$___ daily benefit during hospital confinement · maximum 365 days per confinement · covers accident and sickness</div></div>
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">Outpatient Surgical Indemnity</div><div class="b-val">Daily benefit rate paid as if hospitalized, per a day schedule in the policy. Surgeries not listed are paid a comparable number of days based on severity.</div></div>
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">At-Home Indemnity Benefit</div><div class="b-val">Weekly benefit for medically necessary home health visits. Accrues 1 week per hospital day. Maximum 12 weeks. Must begin within 7 days of discharge. Requires skilled nursing, or physical, speech, hearing, or occupational therapy, prescribed by physician.</div></div>
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">Emergency Accident Benefit</div><div class="b-val">Emergency accident cash for treatment within 72 hours. Not payable if other benefits under this policy apply.</div></div>
            <div class="benefit-item"><div class="b-name">Accidental Death & Dismemberment</div><div class="b-val">Amounts set at policy issue. Payable for loss occurring within 90 days of the accident. In lieu of or reduced by other benefits paid.</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Pre-Existing Condition Provision</div>
          <p>This is the most significant limitation of the H34. No benefits are payable for any loss beginning during the first 2 years of coverage if that loss results from a condition for which the insured received or was recommended medical advice or treatment within the 2-year period immediately preceding the policy effective date. This is a strict 2-year lookback and 2-year exclusion window — agents must disclose this condition clearly to all clients with recent medical histories.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Renewability — Non-Cancellable for Life</div>
          <p>The H34 is the only supplemental that is renewable for the life of the insured with an explicit non-cancellation guarantee. The company cannot cancel, terminate, or decline to renew this policy. Premium rates may only be adjusted on an overall state class basis — never on an individual basis. This represents the strongest renewability provision in the AIL supplemental lineup and is a compelling long-term value argument.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Exclusions & Limitations</div>
          <ul class="exclusion-list">
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>War or any act of war, declared or undeclared</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Intentional self-inflicted injury or suicide</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Mental, nervous, or emotional disorder</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Normal pregnancy, normal childbirth, or abortion</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Committing or attempting to commit a felony or assault</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Air travel, except as fare-paying passenger on a regularly scheduled commercial airline</li>
            <li><span class="excl-mark">✕</span>Pre-existing conditions: losses beginning in first 2 policy years from conditions treated/advised within 2 years prior to effective date</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Optional Rider — BM-200 Recuperation Indemnity</div>
          <p>Provides a weekly recuperation benefit after a period of hospitalization, payable when the covered person is unable to perform regular and customary duties and remains under the regular care of a physician. One week of recuperation benefit is payable for each day of hospitalization, up to a maximum of 12 weeks.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="deep-section">
          <div class="deep-section-title">Agent Field Notes</div>
          <div class="key-points">
            <div class="kp-title">Sales Positioning</div>
            <ul class="kp-list">
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>"Unlike the accident policies, this covers you for anything that puts you in the hospital — a fall, an illness, a surgery — any covered cause"</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>The At-Home benefit is unique in the portfolio: "Every day you're confined in the hospital, you earn one week of covered home health care after discharge"</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>Outpatient surgical indemnity is increasingly relevant as more procedures migrate from inpatient to outpatient settings</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>"This company cannot cancel this policy under any circumstances — as long as you pay the premium, you have coverage for the rest of your life"</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>The 2-year pre-existing lookback and 2-year exclusion window must be disclosed clearly and documented — it is the most common source of client disputes on this product</li>
              <li><span class="kp-mark">◆</span>H34 occupies a unique position in the portfolio — it fills coverage gaps across accident, illness, and surgical causes that all other supplementals leave open</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

  </div><!-- end deep-container -->
